    "created_at": "2025-09-16T17:30:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-09-16T17:30:02Z",
    "body": "You can change it in the middle of a fetch, so I think it's true that redirects could see different user agent headers (you could also do the same thing with request interception). \r\n\r\nIn general I don't think people are expected to change this often for existing traversables; the typical use case is \"set the user agent when creating a top-level traversable and use it for the entire lifetime of that traversable\".\r\n\r\nSo I think I agree that in principle caching the value at the start of a redirect loop is the right thing to do, but in practice it's likely to be a rare edge case.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
